## Parent
- Spec: benchmark-gepa-overhaul
- Goals: G-4, G-5
- Depends on: bench-result-substrate, bench-panel-manifest, bench-model-judge, bench-prompt-files
- Frozen decisions: F-2, F-3, F-4, F-5, F-6

## Problem

Parent goal: Grow the benchmark with FeatureBench, the Gin render-context task, and a few cherry-picked tasks, in a format GEPA can optimize against once-run stored baselines, with a model judge for structural-tool applicability.

This curd is the loop that the other curds feed. The MCP instructions are compiled in (`src/mcp/mod.rs:76`) and byte-locked by a `#[cfg(test)]` test (`src/mcp/mod.rs:771-780`), so a text-only optimizer cannot change what agents see without a rebuild and a lock rewrite. Pinned variants can only be built from a remote git URL (`benchmark/variants.py:96-99`), so a local candidate commit cannot be served today. The stored row carries grader text in `correctness_reason` (`benchmark/run.py:1084`): missing ground-truth strings (`benchmark/tasks/base.py:180`) and up to 1200 characters of held-out test output (`benchmark/tasks/gin_render_context_tasks.py:156-157,165`). The cell loop also prints that reason to stdout (`benchmark/run.py:1658`). A naive reflection step would therefore leak the grader into the model that rewrites tilth. Paired comparison exists (`benchmark/paired.py:141-160,195`), but it joins on task, model, and repetition, so frontier re-runs need frozen baseline rows at the same repetition numbers.

## Contract

The evolution loop (parent curd c5) adds `benchmark/evolve/` and two run.py seams. It changes no file under `src/**` or `prompts/**` itself; only candidate commits on local refs do.

- **Panel and ledger (G-5, F-6).** `evolve.main` obtains its panel only through `panels.load_panel(path, *, store_path, admit=...)`, with `store_path` set to the run.py result store (`RESULTS_DIR / baselines.STORE_FILENAME`, `benchmark/run.py:1474`). It builds one `spend.SpendLedger(max_usd)` (c1 follow-up: `would_cross(estimate)`, `charge(cost, *, source)`, `spent`) and passes that single instance to every cell, judge, reflection, and proposer call. Every cell runs through `run.run_plan(cells, *, panel, ledger, candidate_sha, refreeze_baselines)`, whose signature c3 defines and c5 implements and tests (`bench-panel-manifest.md` run_plan seam). Before planning any cell, it calls `panel.register(TASKS)`; c3's `Panel.register` loads external members through c2 loaders, is idempotent by task digest, and refuses name collisions. It then merges `Panel.stamp(task)` (`panel_name`, `panel_split` equal to the member's tier, and `panel_split_digest` computed from the manifest) into each row before `baselines.store` at `RESULTS_DIR / baselines.STORE_FILENAME`, on the same path run.py uses, so c3's split lock sees evolve rows.
- **Candidate (F-2).** A candidate has five components:
  - four text components: `prompts/mcp.md`, `prompts/tools/read.md`, `prompts/tools/search.md`, and `prompts/tools/write.md`;
  - `src_patch`, a unified diff over `src/**` that is cumulative from `--seed-sha`: it is always the full diff of the candidate's `src/**` against the seed, never an increment on its GEPA parent.
  **Identity.** A candidate's content id is the sha256 of the canonical JSON (sorted keys, UTF-8, no insignificant whitespace) of its five components, and its ref is `evolve/<run-id>/<content-id>` with the first 12 hex digits. The seed candidate holds those four files' bytes at `--seed-sha` and an empty `src_patch`, and its ref points at `--seed-sha` itself. Every other candidate is one commit whose parent is `--seed-sha`. Evolve records a first-seen sequence number the first time it evaluates a content id, and that number is the only candidate order it uses. It never relies on GEPA candidate indices, because gepa 0.1.4 evaluates a child on its minibatch before the child has a pool index (`gepa/proposer/reflective_mutation/reflective_mutation.py:517,533-550`), and a child that fails minibatch acceptance never gets one. Because GEPA builds a child by copying its parent and replacing only the proposed components, a text-only child inherits its parent's whole cumulative `src_patch` and still applies cleanly onto the seed. A candidate's identity in rows is its commit `git_sha` plus the `binary_sha256` of the binary built from it.
- **Engine (F-3).** `evolve.main` drives GEPA `optimize_anything` with the seed candidate, `evolve.evaluate` as the evaluator, the dev split as the dataset, and `--max-metric-calls` as the budget. Verified against `gepa==0.1.4` from PyPI:
  - `optimize_anything(seed_candidate, *, evaluator, dataset, valset, objective, background, config)` takes a `dict[str, str]` seed.
  - GEPA forwards each dataset item to the evaluator only as the keyword `example` and drops keywords the evaluator does not name (`gepa/optimize_anything.py:1002-1044`). The evaluator signature is therefore `evolve.evaluate(candidate, example)`.
  - `GEPAConfig(engine=EngineConfig(max_metric_calls=...))` stops once `total_num_evals` reaches the budget. One metric call is one evaluator call on one (candidate, dev task) pair.
  - GEPA has one proposal hook, `ReflectionConfig.custom_candidate_proposer(candidate, reflective_dataset, components_to_update) -> dict[str, str]`. When set, it owns proposals for every component and GEPA's own `reflection_lm` (default `openai/gpt-5.1` through litellm, which needs an API key) is never called.
  So `engine.py` registers one dispatcher as `custom_candidate_proposer`. For each text component in `components_to_update`, it makes one isolated `claude -p` reflection call through the shared auth guard and spend ledger. For `src_patch`, it calls `evolve.propose_src_patch`. It also registers the stop state below as a `StopperProtocol` in `GEPAConfig.stop_callbacks`. `module_selector` stays `round_robin`, and `raise_on_exception` keeps gepa's default. `benchmark/evolve/engine.py` is the only module that imports `gepa`. Unit tests stub it. The engine-signature, stop, and frontier tests run the real pinned `gepa.optimize_anything`, so gepa behavior drift fails them.
- **Stop state (F-3, F-6).** In gepa 0.1.4 an exception from the proposer does not stop the search. `_propose_texts_batch_safe` catches it, calls the proposer again, and then skips the proposal (`gepa/proposer/reflective_mutation/reflective_mutation.py:203-225`), and the engine moves on to its next iteration (`gepa/core/engine.py:846-849`). So evolve never stops by raising. It keeps one shared stop state with a reason: `ceiling`, `quota`, or `plateau`.
  - A ledger check that would cross the ceiling sets `ceiling`. A usage-limit rejection in any call (cell, judge, reflection, proposer) sets `quota`. The plateau counter sets `plateau`.
  - The registered `StopperProtocol` returns True once the state is set, which ends `optimize_anything`.
  - While the state is set, the dispatcher returns the parent's components unchanged without a model call, and `evaluate` returns score 0 with side info `stopped: <reason>` without a model call, so gepa's retry and any evaluation still in flight cost nothing.
  - After `ceiling` or `quota` is set, no paid call of any kind starts again in that evolve run, finish included.
- **Reflection isolation (F-5).** A text-component reflection call runs like a c4 judge call. It runs in a fresh, empty temporary cwd with a fresh, empty temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and authenticates only through `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in its env. Its argv carries `--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, `--setting-sources ""`, and no `--mcp-config` or `--bare`. The prompt goes on stdin and holds only the component's current text and the reflective records. With no tools, it cannot read `benchmark/` files, the panel, or the harness data directory, and no user hook or MCP server loads.
- **Reflective record (G-4, F-5).** For each cheap-tier or paid-tier dev rollout, `evolve.evaluate` builds one record as `judge.stripped_record(row, sidecar)`, c4's single stripped record. It holds the task prompt, c4's allowlisted row fields, and the untruncated trajectory sidecar. c4 owns the allowlist, and c5 defines none of its own. The record never holds `correctness_reason`, the ground-truth definition, gold patches, or held-out test source or output. Agent-produced text stays verbatim even when it matches a ground-truth string, since a correct answer to `rg_trait_implementors` must name `Matcher`, `find_at`, and `RegexMatcher` (`benchmark/tasks/ripgrep_tasks.py:26`). When the judge is calibrated, c5 adds exactly two keys to that dict: `label` (the task's cached applicability label) and `critique`. The critique is `judge.critique(row, trajectory)`, called on the raw stored row and its sidecar; c4 strips them internally with the same `stripped_record`, refuses contaminated or unscanned rows, and caches by `run_key`. The reflection prompt, the proposer prompt, and the cheap-tier and paid-tier side info are built only from these records.
- **Excluded rollouts (F-5).** A rollout whose row has `contaminated: true` yields no record, and c5 makes no critique call for it. A row with no `contaminated` key stops the run with an error naming the row, rather than being scored. No test-split rollout ever yields a record, critique, side info entry, or proposer input; test-split cells run only inside `evolve.finish`.
- **Score (F-5).** A candidate's score is the mean grader `correct` over its paid-tier dev rollouts, with a contaminated rollout counted as incorrect. For each `example`, `evolve.evaluate` returns that dev task's mean `correct` over the candidate's rollouts as GEPA's per-instance score. Cheap-tier rollouts, test-split rollouts, applicability labels, and critiques never change it.
- **Judge gating (F-5).** Before any paid cell, `evolve.main` builds one c4 `Judge` with the run's shared ledger. It obtains a cached `judge.applicability` label for every panel task and calls `judge.calibrate`, logging the agreement value. When any panel task ends the preflight without a valid cached label, for example because c4 raised `JudgeAnswerInvalid`, evolve refuses the run before any paid cell and names each such task. When the judge is calibrated, records carry `label` and `critique`, and the delta report adds per-label accuracy slices. When it is not, records carry neither, no critique call is made, and the run log and delta report say `labels: uncalibrated`. A judge answer outside c4's categorical label set yields no cached label.
  - **Critique failures stay inside `evaluate`.** When `judge.critique` raises `CritiqueRejected`, `CritiqueWithheld`, or any other judge error, the record keeps no `critique`, gains `critique_error: <reason>`, and evaluation continues. `JudgeQuota` also sets the stop state to `quota`. `evaluate` catches every judge error itself, so gepa's default `raise_on_exception=True` (`gepa/optimize_anything.py:468`) never sees one.
- **Proposer isolation (F-2, F-5).** `evolve.propose_src_patch(worktree, records)` runs `claude -p` in an export that is the candidate's own tree: a `git archive` export of `src/**`, `prompts/**`, `Cargo.toml`, and `Cargo.lock` at `--seed-sha`, with the candidate's text components written and its cumulative `src_patch` applied. The export sits in a temp directory outside the tilth checkout, with no `.git`.
  - The argv passes `--tools Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep`, disallows `Bash`, `WebFetch`, `WebSearch`, `Agent`, and `Task`, and carries `--strict-mcp-config` and `--setting-sources ""` with no `--mcp-config`.
  - `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` is a per-call temp dir that holds only the copied auth file, as `_cell_claude_config` does (`benchmark/run.py:425`).
  - The returned diff is the new cumulative diff of the export's `src/**` against the seed's `src/**`, including the parent's hunks. Edits outside `src/**` are dropped and logged.
  - The proposal is rejected when any proposer tool call's input resolves to a path outside the export, or any tool input or output names `benchmark/`, the panel file path or basename, or the harness data directory. On rejection nothing is committed, and the dispatcher returns the parent's `src_patch` unchanged for that component, so the rejection alone creates no new content id or cell. At HEAD no file under `src/` or `prompts/` contains the string `benchmark/`.
- **Applier (F-2, F-4).** `evolve.materialize(candidate)` is memoized by content id. The first call for a content id works in a git worktree of the tilth repo at `--seed-sha` and runs the steps below in order. Every later call for that content id, from any `evaluate` call, returns the same sha without touching git.
  1. write the four text components;
  2. apply the cumulative `src_patch`;
  3. reject the candidate when any path changed against the seed is outside `src/**` and `prompts/**`, or any changed line sits inside a `#[cfg(test)]` item, or in a file that is itself a `#[cfg(test)]` module such as `src/edit/integration_tests.rs` (declared at `src/edit/mod.rs:14-15`);
  4. regenerate `AGENTS.md` with `scripts/regen-agents-md.sh`;
  5. rewrite the byte-count, `starts_with`, and `ends_with` literals of `server_instructions_byte_lock` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:774,777-780`) to the new `prompts/mcp.md` byte length, its leading lines (as many as the current literal spans), and its last line;
  6. commit with parent `--seed-sha`, point `evolve/<run-id>/<content-id>` at that commit, and return the sha.
  Every other `#[cfg(test)]` guard stays a guard that `just check` enforces: the remaining byte-lock assertions, `cwd_guidance_spans_present` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:2292`), the 2KB instruction checks (`src/mcp/mod.rs:1245-1250,2305`), `agents_md_matches_prompt_sources` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:1230`), the 13,779-byte surface cap (`src/mcp/mod.rs:816`), and `tool_descriptions_fit_2kb` (`src/mcp/tools/definitions.rs:524`).
- **Cascade (F-3, F-4).** `evolve.cascade(sha)` runs four stages. It stops at the first failure with score 0 and the failing stage recorded in side info. The apply result, the `just check` result, and the binary build are memoized per content id alongside the commit. So repeated `evaluate` calls for one candidate on different examples reuse one commit, one `git_sha` and `binary_sha256`, and one `just check` result, and their cells keep stable run keys that the store answers.
  1. apply (materialize succeeded);
  2. `just check` in the candidate worktree;
  3. cheap tier: the panel's cheap tasks, one rollout each; it passes when the candidate's cheap-tier correctness is at least the seed's;
  4. paid tier: every dev task.
  Side info for an apply or `just check` failure holds the stage name and the failing tail of that stage's output. That output is tilth build and test output, which carries no grader material. Side info for the cheap and paid tiers holds only the stage name, the per-task scores, and the records built with `judge.stripped_record`. It never holds run.py stdout or stderr, or any row field outside the stripped record. Cells run through `run.run_plan` with `--candidate-sha`, which builds the tilth binary with `cargo build --release --locked` at that commit and records its `git_sha` and `binary_sha256` in the row's variant metadata (`benchmark/run.py:91-108`). The seed's cheap-tier and paid-tier rows come from the store when present.
- **Baselines (G-5).** The baseline arm is mode `baseline` (`benchmark/config.py:142-148`).
  - The first evolve run over a panel buys each baseline cell once: every dev and cheap task at repetitions 1 to 1 + R, where R is the re-run count.
  - Later runs, and every candidate in a run, answer those cells from the c1 store and write them to the run's output JSONL with `reused: true`.
  - c1's drift refusal applies: a planned baseline cell with a completed row only under a different key refuses the run unless `--refreeze-baselines` is passed, which buys each drifted cell once under the new key.
  - Test-split baseline cells are bought the same way, once, inside `evolve.finish`.
- **Accepted frontier (F-3).** Evolve keeps its own accepted frontier, separate from gepa's internal Pareto front.
  - **Re-runs.** When a candidate has a first rollout on every dev task and that per-task vector is not dominated by any accepted member, it is re-run R more times on every dev task at repetitions 2 to 1 + R. Those repetitions give fresh run keys, so the store never answers a re-run with the first rollout.
  - **Acceptance.** It is accepted only when all R re-runs completed and its per-task means over 1 + R rollouts are not dominated by any accepted member; accepted members it dominates leave. From then on, `evaluate` returns those means to GEPA. A dominated candidate is neither re-run nor accepted.
  - **GEPA's front is never read.** gepa 0.1.4 adds any candidate that ties the best score on an instance to that instance's Pareto front (`gepa/core/state.py:496-508`), and ties at 0 or 1 are routine with grader correctness. So GEPA's front can hold a single-rollout candidate; `evolve.finish` reads only the accepted frontier, so such a candidate is never a finalist.
- **Delta report (G-5).** For every candidate that reaches the paid tier, `evolve` writes a delta report to the run log. It is computed with `paired.paired_accuracy_delta` and `paired.paired_cpc_delta` over the candidate's tilth rows and the stored baseline rows at the same task, model, and repetition. Building it never invokes a baseline-arm runner.
- **Stop and finish (F-4).** The search ends when `--max-metric-calls` is spent or when the stop state is set: `plateau` after P consecutive paid-tier candidates leave the best accepted-frontier dev mean unimproved, or `ceiling` or `quota`. `evolve.finish(accepted_frontier)` then runs in every case.
  - **Finalists.** The finalists are the two non-seed accepted-frontier candidates with the highest dev mean over 1 + R rollouts, plus the seed. Each finalist is scored once on the test split at repetitions 1 to 1 + R. After a `ceiling` or `quota` stop, finish starts no paid call: it uses only test-split rows the store already holds, and when any finalist lacks one, it logs `finish: incomplete (<reason>)` with the scores it has and opens no PR.
  - **Winner.** The winner is the finalist with the highest test-split mean correctness, with contaminated rollouts counted incorrect. Ties go to the higher dev mean, then to the lower first-seen sequence number.
  - **Seed wins.** When the winner is the seed, finish opens no PR and logs `no improvement`.
  - **Non-seed winner.** Finish pushes only the winner commit, as the branch `evolve/<run-id>-winner`. It then opens exactly one draft PR with base `--base-branch` (the branch `--seed-sha` came from, default `main`) and head `evolve/<run-id>-winner`, whose body holds the winner's dev and test delta reports. It refuses to push or open the PR when the seed-to-winner diff touches a path outside `src/**`, `prompts/**`, and `AGENTS.md`, or when the winner's cascade record lacks a `just check` pass. It never merges and never enables auto-merge.
- **Spend and auth (F-6).** `evolve.main` requires `--max-usd` and exits before any model call without it. The one `spend.SpendLedger` instance spans every paid call in the run: agent cells, judge calls, reflection calls, and proposer calls.
  - Each call first passes the shared auth guard, which refuses it when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set. It then passes `SpendLedger.would_cross(estimate)`; when that is true, the call does not start and the stop state is set to `ceiling`.
  - A cell's estimate follows c1's tiers.
  - A judge call's estimate is c4's canonical rule, applied inside the `Judge`; evolve passes the `Judge` the ledger and the `--cell-estimate-usd` floor and defines no judge estimate of its own.
  - A reflection or proposer call's estimate is the mean cost of earlier calls of the same kind (reflection or proposer) in this run, else `--cell-estimate-usd`.
  - A usage-limit rejection in any call sets the stop state to `quota` and writes `infra:quota` to the run log, leaving stored rows reusable. The run log and delta reports carry no task-growth gate verdict.
- **Agent-decided defaults.**
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] R = 3 re-runs and plateau P = 5, flags `--reruns` and `--plateau`; this settles the parent open question. A plateau round counts only candidates that reach the paid tier, so a streak of build failures does not end the search. Alternative: count every proposed candidate.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] One model per evolve run, `--model` defaulting to `haiku` because the repo guidance tests instruction changes on haiku. Alternative: `sonnet`, the `run.py` default.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] The proposer works in a `git archive` export with no `.git`, a stricter form of the parent's sparse worktree, so no git metadata links back to the full checkout. Alternative: `git worktree add` with sparse checkout.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] A row missing the `contaminated` key stops the run. Alternative: count it as contaminated and continue.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] `--candidate-sha` builds from the local commit instead of going through an experiment manifest, because `benchmark/variants.py:96-99` admits only remote git URLs. Alternative: relax that check to accept `file://`.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] Cheap-tier dev rollouts also yield reflective records, so reflection sees why a candidate failed the cheap tier. Alternative: paid-tier records only.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] After a `ceiling` or `quota` stop, finish scores only from stored test-split rows and opens no PR when any is missing. Alternative: let finish buy the missing test cells under whatever ceiling remains.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] `evolve.main` refuses to start when `--seed-sha` is not an ancestor of `--base-branch`, so the draft PR diff is exactly seed to winner. Alternative: open the PR against any base and let the reviewer rebase.

## Grounding

| Probe | Outcome | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| wiki | hit | `.hallouminate/wiki/mcp-instructions-limits-and-format.md`: `prompts/mcp.md` is one byte-locked file of at most 2,048 chars and tool descriptions are truncated at 2,048 chars each, so the cascade `just check` stage is the size guard; `.hallouminate/wiki/benchmark-harness-gotchas.md`: a stale installed binary served old instructions for weeks, so candidate cells must build from the candidate commit and record `binary_sha256` |
| explorer | hit | HEAD `806ea7b` read with `git show`: `SERVER_INSTRUCTIONS` via `include_str!` at `src/mcp/mod.rs:76`, byte lock at `src/mcp/mod.rs:771-780` (1966 bytes, `starts_with` two lines, `ends_with` last line), all three tool descriptions loaded by `include_str!` from `prompts/tools/*.md` at `src/mcp/tools/definitions.rs:4-6` since `9afcd8b`; `SpendLedger` with `would_cross` and `charge` in `benchmark/spend.py`; `scripts/regen-agents-md.sh` writes a header plus `prompts/mcp.md`; `paired.py` pairs on task, model, repetition (`paired.py:141-160`); variants require remote URLs (`variants.py:96-99`); `correctness_reason` at `run.py:1084` and printed at `run.py:1658`; file-level test module at `src/edit/mod.rs:14-15`; `gepa==0.1.4`: evaluator keyword forwarding at `gepa/optimize_anything.py:1002-1044`, child evaluated before it has a pool index at `reflective_mutation.py:517,533-550`, proposer exceptions retried then skipped at `reflective_mutation.py:203-225` and `core/engine.py:846-849`, ties joining the Pareto front at `core/state.py:496-508` |

## Approach

1. **Engine skeleton and seed (F-3, F-2).** Add `benchmark/evolve/` with `engine.py` as the only `gepa` importer, and pin `gepa==0.1.4` in `benchmark/requirements.txt`. `evolve.main` loads the panel with `panels.load_panel(path, *, store_path, admit=...)` against the run.py store, reads the seed's four text components at `--seed-sha`, and refuses when any is missing. It passes the seed candidate, `evolve.evaluate(candidate, example)`, and `--max-metric-calls` to `optimize_anything`, with the component dispatcher as `custom_candidate_proposer` and the stop state as a `StopperProtocol` in `stop_callbacks`.
2. **Spend and auth first (F-6).** `evolve.main` builds one `spend.SpendLedger(max_usd)` from `--max-usd`. Every cell, reflection, and proposer call goes through the shared auth guard and that ledger. The c4 `Judge` gets the same ledger and applies its own canonical estimate. A crossing estimate or a quota rejection anywhere sets the shared stop state, which ends the search through the stop callback and neutralizes gepa's retries.
3. **Records and judge gating (F-5, G-4).** Build reflective records with `judge.stripped_record`, drop contaminated and test-split rollouts, run the judge preflight (refusing any task without a valid label), add `label` and `critique` only when calibrated, and record `critique_error` instead of raising. Run reflection calls toolless in an empty cwd and config dir.
4. **Proposer and applier (F-2, F-4, F-5).** `propose_src_patch` runs the isolated proposer on the candidate's tree, scans its trajectory, and returns the cumulative diff against the seed. On rejection, the dispatcher returns the parent's `src_patch`. `materialize`, memoized by content id, applies text and cumulative patch onto the seed, enforces the allowlist and the `#[cfg(test)]` guard, regenerates `AGENTS.md`, rewrites the byte-lock literals, and commits on the ref `evolve/<run-id>/<content-id>`.
5. **Cascade, baselines, and frontier (F-3, F-4, G-5).** Add `run.run_plan`, which calls `panel.register(TASKS)` before planning and stamps every row with the panel before `baselines.store`, and `--candidate-sha`. `cascade` runs apply, `just check`, the cheap tier, and the paid tier, with grader-free side info, buying baselines once and reusing them. Memoize apply, `just check`, and the build per content id. Re-run non-dominated candidates R times on fresh repetitions into evolve's own accepted frontier, and write a paired delta report for each paid-tier candidate.
6. **Finish (F-4, F-2).** On every stop, take finalists from the accepted frontier, score them once on the test split (stored rows only after a ceiling or quota stop), and pick the winner by the tie rule. For a non-seed winner, push only the winner branch and open one draft PR through a PR client seam (`gh pr create --draft --base <base-branch> --head evolve/<run-id>-winner`).

## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            NEW SLICE benchmark/evolve/ + benchmark (existing harness)
spine step:       entry (evolve.main) + workflow (cascade, finish) + infra (materialize, proposer export, reflection client)
public interface: evolve.main(--panel PATH, --max-usd FLOAT, --max-metric-calls INT, --seed-sha SHA, --base-branch NAME, --model NAME, --reruns INT, --plateau INT, --cell-estimate-usd FLOAT, --refreeze-baselines)  (F-3, F-6)
public interface: evolve.evaluate(candidate, example) -> (score, side_info)  (F-3, F-5)
public interface: evolve.propose_src_patch(worktree, records) -> diff (cumulative against --seed-sha)  (F-2, F-5)
public interface: evolve.materialize(candidate) -> sha (memoized by content id; commit on --seed-sha at ref evolve/<run-id>/<content-id>)  (F-2, F-4)
public interface: evolve.cascade(sha) -> (score, side_info)  (F-3, F-4)
public interface: evolve.finish(accepted_frontier) -> PullRequest | None (base --base-branch, head evolve/<run-id>-winner)  (F-4)
public interface: run.run_plan(cells, *, panel: Panel, ledger: SpendLedger, candidate_sha, refreeze_baselines) -> list[Row], calling panel.register(TASKS) before planning and stamping each row before baselines.store (signature defined in bench-panel-manifest.md); run.py --candidate-sha SHA  (F-2, F-6, G-5)
consumed:         baselines.lookup / baselines.store, spend.SpendLedger(max_usd) with would_cross, charge, spent, and the auth guard (c1); panels.load_panel(path, *, store_path, admit) -> Panel(cheap, dev, test) Panel.register(tasks), and Panel.stamp(task) (c3); Judge(ledger, ...), judge.stripped_record(row, sidecar) -> dict, judge.applicability(task) -> Label, judge.critique(row, trajectory) -> str, judge.calibrate(labels) -> Agreement (c4); paired.paired_accuracy_delta, paired.paired_cpc_delta; gepa.optimize_anything 0.1.4
private:          component dispatcher, reflection client, and StopperProtocol stop state (engine.py), content-id hashing and materialize memo, accepted frontier, proposer trajectory scan, cfg(test) span detector, byte-lock literal rewriter, dominance check, plateau counter, finalist and winner selection by first-seen sequence, reflection and proposer estimate tiers, PR client
crust delta:      new package benchmark/evolve/; new run.py function run_plan and flag --candidate-sha; gepa==0.1.4 pinned in benchmark/requirements.txt; evolve run log under benchmark/results/evolve/<run-id>/
arrows:           evolve -> run, baselines, panels, judge, paired; engine -> gepa; no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Acceptance
- AC-1: WHEN evolve builds a reflective record for a cheap-tier or paid-tier dev rollout THE SYSTEM SHALL build it as `judge.stripped_record(row, sidecar)` over the stored JSONL row and its untruncated trajectory sidecar, with every tool call's full input and output and the agent's final answer verbatim even when they contain a ground-truth string and no `correctness_reason`, ground-truth definition, gold patch, or held-out test text, adding only the `label` and `critique` keys when calibrated, SHALL obtain each critique by calling `judge.critique` on the raw stored row and its sidecar, and SHALL build reflection prompts, proposer prompts, and cheap-tier and paid-tier side info only from those records.  (G-4, F-5)
- AC-2: WHEN a rollout is contaminated THE SYSTEM SHALL build no reflective record and make no critique call for it, WHEN a rollout belongs to the test split THE SYSTEM SHALL never put it in a record, critique, side info entry, or proposer input, and WHEN a dev rollout is neither THE SYSTEM SHALL build exactly one record for it.  (F-5, G-4)
- AC-3: WHEN the cascade scores a candidate that reaches the paid tier THE SYSTEM SHALL return the mean grader `correct` over its paid-tier dev rollouts as the only score, counting a contaminated rollout as incorrect, unchanged by any applicability label, critique, cheap-tier row, or test-split row, and WHEN a scored row lacks the `contaminated` key THE SYSTEM SHALL stop the run with an error naming that row.  (F-5, F-3)
- AC-4: WHEN an evolve run starts THE SYSTEM SHALL obtain a cached categorical applicability label for every panel task and log the judge agreement value before any paid cell, and SHALL refuse the run before any paid cell, naming each task, when any task lacks a valid label; WHEN the judge is calibrated THE SYSTEM SHALL attach each task label and rollout critique to its reflective record and slice the delta report by label, and WHEN a critique call raises THE SYSTEM SHALL leave that record without a critique, record `critique_error`, and continue without raising out of `evaluate`; WHEN it is uncalibrated THE SYSTEM SHALL attach neither, make no critique call, and mark the run log and delta report uncalibrated.  (F-5)
- AC-5: WHEN evolve proposes a `src_patch` THE SYSTEM SHALL run the proposer in an export of the candidate's own tree (seed plus its text components and cumulative `src_patch`) holding only `src/**`, `prompts/**`, `Cargo.toml`, and `Cargo.lock` with no `.git`, with Bash and web tools disabled, `--strict-mcp-config` and `--setting-sources ""` set, no MCP config, and a config dir holding only auth, SHALL return the new cumulative `src/**` diff against the seed, and WHEN any proposer tool input resolves outside the export or any tool input or output names `benchmark/`, the panel file, or the harness data directory THE SYSTEM SHALL commit nothing and return the parent's `src_patch` unchanged.  (F-2, F-5)
- AC-6: WHEN evolve materializes a candidate THE SYSTEM SHALL, in a worktree at `--seed-sha`, write the text components, apply the cumulative patch, reject any change outside `src/**` and `prompts/**` or inside a `#[cfg(test)]` item or `#[cfg(test)]` module file, regenerate `AGENTS.md`, rewrite the byte-count, `starts_with`, and `ends_with` literals of `server_instructions_byte_lock` to match the new `prompts/mcp.md`, and only then commit with parent `--seed-sha` on the ref `evolve/<run-id>/<content-id>`, where the content id is the sha256 of the candidate's canonical component JSON, so a text-only child of a patched parent materializes and builds; WHEN a content id is materialized again THE SYSTEM SHALL return the same sha without a new commit.  (F-2, F-4)
- AC-7: WHEN a candidate commit exists THE SYSTEM SHALL evaluate it through apply, `just check`, the cheap tier (passing when its cheap-tier correctness is at least the seed's), then the paid tier, SHALL stop at the first failing stage with score 0 and that stage recorded, SHALL put a failing stage's output tail in side info only for the apply and `just check` stages and only stripped records for the cheap and paid tiers, SHALL run apply, `just check`, and the binary build once per content id so repeated `evaluate` calls for one candidate reuse one commit, `git_sha`, `binary_sha256`, and `just check` result, and SHALL serve candidate cells from that binary with its `git_sha` and `binary_sha256` in the row.  (F-3, F-4, F-5)
- AC-8: WHEN the first evolve run over a panel starts on an empty store THE SYSTEM SHALL make exactly one baseline-arm runner call per baseline cell, WHEN a later run over an unchanged panel, agent CLI, and env fingerprint runs THE SYSTEM SHALL make no baseline-arm runner call and write those rows to its output JSONL with `reused: true`, and WHEN a baseline cell drifted to a different key THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse to start unless `--refreeze-baselines` is passed, after which it buys that cell once under the new key; and every row evolve stores SHALL carry `panel_name`, `panel_split_digest`, and `panel_split` from the panel loaded through `panels.load_panel` against the run.py store, with `panel_split` equal to the member's tier, stamped before `baselines.store`, after `run.run_plan` has called `panel.register(TASKS)` before planning any cell.  (G-5, F-3)
- AC-9: WHEN a candidate has a first rollout on every dev task and that vector is not dominated by evolve's accepted frontier THE SYSTEM SHALL re-run it R times on every dev task at fresh repetitions and accept it only when all re-runs completed and its per-task means are not dominated, WHEN it is dominated THE SYSTEM SHALL neither re-run nor accept it, WHEN a candidate reaches the paid tier THE SYSTEM SHALL write a paired delta report of accuracy and cost per correct against stored baseline rows without a baseline-arm runner call, and WHEN P consecutive paid-tier candidates leave the best accepted dev mean unimproved THE SYSTEM SHALL set the stop state to `plateau`.  (F-3, G-5)
- AC-10: WHEN the search ends THE SYSTEM SHALL run finish on evolve's accepted frontier and never on GEPA's Pareto front, SHALL score once on the test split the two non-seed accepted candidates with the highest dev mean plus the seed, SHALL pick as winner the finalist with the highest test-split mean, breaking ties by higher dev mean and then lower first-seen sequence number, and WHEN the winner is not the seed SHALL push only the winner commit as branch `evolve/<run-id>-winner` and open exactly one draft PR with base `--base-branch` and head that branch, whose commit passed `just check`, whose seed-to-winner diff touches only `src/**`, `prompts/**`, and `AGENTS.md`, and whose body holds the delta reports, and SHALL never merge it; WHEN the seed wins THE SYSTEM SHALL push nothing and open no PR; WHEN the search ended on a `ceiling` or `quota` stop THE SYSTEM SHALL start no paid call in finish and open no PR unless every finalist's test-split rows are already stored.  (F-4, F-2)
- AC-11: WHEN an evolve run starts without `--max-usd` THE SYSTEM SHALL exit before any model call; WHEN any agent cell, judge call, reflection call, or proposer call starts THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse it with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set, count its cost against the one run-wide ceiling, and not start a call whose estimate would cross it, estimating judge calls only by c4's canonical rule and reflection and proposer calls by the same-kind mean in this run else `--cell-estimate-usd`; WHEN the next call would cross the ceiling or any call reports a usage-limit rejection THE SYSTEM SHALL set the shared stop state, end `optimize_anything` through the registered stop callback, start no further paid call in that run, and while the state is set return the parent's components from the dispatcher and score 0 from `evaluate` without a model call; and the run log SHALL carry no task-growth gate verdict.  (F-6, F-3)
- AC-12: WHEN an evolve run starts THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse before any model call if any of `prompts/mcp.md`, `prompts/tools/read.md`, `prompts/tools/search.md`, or `prompts/tools/write.md` is missing at `--seed-sha`, and otherwise SHALL call GEPA `optimize_anything` with a seed candidate holding those four files' bytes and an empty `src_patch`, `evolve.evaluate(candidate, example)` as evaluator, the dev split as dataset, `--max-metric-calls` as `EngineConfig.max_metric_calls`, the stop state as a `StopperProtocol` in `GEPAConfig.stop_callbacks`, and one dispatcher as `ReflectionConfig.custom_candidate_proposer` that routes text components to the isolated `claude -p` reflection call and `src_patch` to `evolve.propose_src_patch`, so no litellm or API-key reflection model is ever called.  (F-3, F-2)
- AC-13: WHEN the dispatcher makes a text-component reflection call THE SYSTEM SHALL run it in a fresh empty temporary cwd with a fresh empty temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, authenticate only through `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in its env, pass `--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, and `--setting-sources ""` with no `--mcp-config` or `--bare`, and send the prompt, built only from the component text and the reflective records, on stdin.  (F-5, F-3)

